# GPT-Realtime-Whisper — findings by Mimo v2.6 Flash (EXCLUDED — no verified benchmarks)

- Source: OpenAI (`gpt-realtime-whisper`)
- Date: 2026-09-29 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

> **Self-exclusion:** zero verified public benchmark numbers were found for this exact model/ID — every benchmark row below reads "no verified public score found". This file is saved as `.excluded` so `pnpm sync` skips it; no scores below are used in averages.

## Model card

- **Name:** GPT-Realtime-Whisper (also documented by Microsoft as **GPT Realtime Transcribe**)
- **Short description:** OpenAI's streaming speech-to-text model for the Realtime API — transcribes live audio as the speaker talks instead of waiting for utterance completion, with a tunable latency/accuracy delay knob. Text-only output: it is an STT leg meant to run alongside `gpt-realtime-translate` (source-language transcript) or a speech-to-speech session, not an agent. Same 2026-05-07 Realtime trio as `gpt-realtime-2` and `gpt-realtime-translate`.
- **Provider / access:** OpenAI Realtime API — the transcription endpoint `v1/realtime/transcription_sessions` only (official endpoint table marks Realtime, translation, Chat Completions, Responses, Live, `v1/audio/transcriptions` etc. as **not supported**; supported feature: `streaming`). Microsoft Foundry/Azure OpenAI hosts it as a Global Standard pay-as-you-go deployment (Azure include `gpt-realtime-whisper.md`, updated 2026-07-27); offline file transcription is explicitly routed to `gpt-transcribe` instead.
- **Release / knowledge:** 2026-05-07 (OpenAI "Advancing voice intelligence with new models in the API"; Reuters 2026-05-07; OpenAI community topic 1380471). Knowledge cutoff: Sep 30, 2024 (official model page).
- **IDs:** `gpt-realtime-whisper` (OpenAI / Azure deployment name). **No OpenCode Zen Free ID** (Zen model list checked 2026-09-29: no `whisper` id).
- **Context window:** 16,000 tokens, 2,000 max output tokens (official model page).
- **Modalities:** audio and text in; text out (official model page). Reasoning: no. Tool calls: no. JSON mode: not listed.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-09-29):** **$0.017 per minute of audio** — duration-billed, not token-billed (official model page + launch post). Azure prices it hourly on the Audio Models rate card. Tier limits run 100 → 1,300 minutes-of-audio per minute by rate-limit tier. Paid, no free tier.
- **Architecture:** proprietary streaming Whisper successor; parameters not disclosed (the classic `whisper-1` remains a separate, non-streaming file-transcription model).

